  I've used adjust, but the problem I encounter most often is
early in the game when I only have one stack of (relatively)
good daggers.  They're completely unidentified, except that
I've deduced through observation that they're not cursed.


  So I adjust them to 'w' (to make wielding fast & sure):

  #adjust
  <whatever they were picked up as>
  w

  - Name them Wield:

  #name
  y
  w
  Wield

  - Drop one

  d1w

  - Rename them as Quiver:

  #name
  y
  w
  Quiver

  - #adjust them to Q for quick & sure requivering:  

  #adjust
  w
  Q

  - Quiver them:

  QQ

  - pick up the one I dropped:

  ,

  - #adjust the singleton back to 'w' (if necessary)

  #adjust
  <x, or whatever>
  w



  Okay, so what's the problem?  

  When I pick up more daggers of the same buc id & enchantment 
(probably uncursed +0), the new daggers get added to my wielded 
'w' stack and not the 'f'ireable 'Q' stack.

  (This seems due to Nethack's apparently general policy of
searching in a-zA-Z order.  See autoquiver.)


  So I have to drop one of the wielded stack, rename the wielded
stack to " ", #adjust the wielded stack to 'Q' (to merge the
stacks), then pick up & rewield my Wield dagger again.  So even
the very useful #adjust doesn't solve everything.



  A possible solution would be to never automatically add a picked
up stackable weapon to a wielded stack.  (In my young and foolish
Nethack youth I once ended up wielding a stack of 20 or so daggers.)


  Of course, the problem goes away as soon as I get a non-cursed
plain/elven dagger that doesn't stack with the rest.


